---
// /resume, "At Work": Alex's own words on each place he has worked,
// hand-written here (source: Me_at_work.md). The record itself is the PDF.
// Its text styles (the page head's rule, sections, items) live below.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
import { APP_ROUTES } from "../config/site.js";

const external = { target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" };
---

<BaseLayout
    title="At Work — Alex Gao"
    description="alex gao (alexgaoth) — professional work and experience."
    keywords={[
        "Alex Gao",
        "alexgaoth",
        "resume",
        "Hypercubic",
        "IBM",
        "Signalor",
    ]}
    path={APP_ROUTES.resume}
>
    <ContentPage>
        <div class="page-head">
            <h1 class="title-page">At Work</h1>
            <p class="caption">
                my resume is{" "}
                <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="https://alexgaoth.com/resume.pdf"
                    {...external}
                >
                    here
                </a>
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <h2 class="section-heading">experience</h2>
            <p class="caption">
                rather than just re-rendering my resume into the DOM, below
                is what i thought about each experience
            </p>

            <article class="item">
                <h3 class="item-title">Hypercubic</h3>
                <p>
                    Working here match almost exactly to what i imagined. An
                    early stage startup that moving at terminal velocity.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Burning tokens at a rate where most dont in a month or
                    many, I was still surprised at the amount of work i get
                    done per day. Other than scoping and architecting the
                    actual work, most of the thinking is a continuous search
                    of bottlenecks.
                </p>
                <p>
                    It is the increasing the change of acceleration, what i
                    call on the job, increasing the{" "}
                    <a
                        class="text-link"
                        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerk_(physics)"
                        {...external}
                    >
                        jerk
                    </a>
                </p>
                <p>
                    I liked our office. The mold allegation might be true or
                    might not be, but I dont really feel it.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="item">
                <h3 class="item-title">IBM</h3>
                <!-- prettier-ignore -->
                <p>
                    The campus of <a class="text-link" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=555+Bailey+Avenue%2C+San+Jose%2C+CA" {...external}>555 Bailey Avenue</a>, and it's surrounding hills, lives in my mind as the
                    definition of what dry California look like.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The campus doesn't have free catering (paid ones are
                    unanimously tasteless), so I had to source my own food.
                </p>
                <p>
                    so apologies to the 10 group lunch and 5 potlucks I have
                    invaded.
                </p>
                <p>People here, especially my team, are very nice.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="item">
                <h3 class="item-title">Signalor</h3>
                <p>
                    I have noticed that most (practically all) of my
                    intellectually rigorous, high agency friend have the
                    intuitive thought about a world where everyone is a
                    founder (albeit many of them aren't one). Most of them
                    would dismiss it with various reasons, but why they felt
                    it to begin with, is revealing.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Founding a company, as it might be cliche to the pg
                    essay readers, is one of the most rewarding thing a
                    person can do in their life. Out of altruistic
                    intentions, many would wish this on the rest of the
                    population.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I dont hide this, Signalor was founded from the wrong
                    heuristic, me and matthieu we just wanted to build,
                    however that doesn't mean I don't believe in this
                    venture. The people always come before the idea, and
                    what we did the past year deems nothing but success for
                    Signalor in the future.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
    </ContentPage>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    /* /resume's text: Grotesk headings, mono text, a 2px rule under the page
       head, a faint line between items. Spacing steps: 8, 16, 24, 32, 48. */
    .page-head {
        padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
        border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
    }
    .page-head .title-page {
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .caption {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.5rem;
        color: #666;
    }
    .section {
        margin-top: 3rem;
    }
    .section-heading,
    .item-title {
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #000;
        text-transform: lowercase;
    }
    .section-heading {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        line-height: 2rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    }
    .item {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        padding-top: 2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    }
    .item-title {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
        line-height: 1.75rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    }
    .item p {
        margin-top: 1rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.5rem;
        color: #222;
    }
    .item-title + p {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }
    .text-link {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    }
    .text-link:hover {
        background: #000;
        color: #fff;
    }
</style>
